{"title":"Two poles formula","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Theorem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proof_using_similar_triangles\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof using similar triangles</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Coordinate/analytical_geometry_proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Coordinate/analytical geometry proof</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Image_Credit\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Image Credit</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Theorem\">Theorem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Two_poles_formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Theorem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The two pole formula/theorem states that for two poles some distance apart, the height of the intersection point of the lines joining the top of either pole to the foot of the opposite pole is half the harmonic mean of the heights of the two poles(and that this is true regardless of the distance between the two poles). \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_using_similar_triangles\">Proof using similar triangles</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Two_poles_formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof using similar triangles\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Image002_1379935198546.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/1/15/Image002_1379935198546.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"269\" height=\"272\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>We are looking to show that for the two poles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> of heights <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> units apart, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b35176848ff12b2a336e6d3c3077fba1c13bc05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{2}{\\frac{1}{a}+\\frac{1}{b}}=\\frac{ab}{a+b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"179\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd937a3ee9efbccaf47bf683c951d5192738204e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ECF} \\sim \\triangle{ACB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57cbf73dfd41475bf786fe2a2c96a44329f35034.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{h}{x}=\\frac{b}{p}\\]\" width=\"48\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/b/eeb4e361add975a1d241d0b3a1a4793e8d9332be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\frac{hp}{b}.\\]\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/2658c4c71731fdfe0a2f061629ba295518ecea81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{EBF} \\sim \\triangle{DBC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f54def8e206027a72691952d2fe16d75f1d96016.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{h}{p-x}=\\frac{a}{p}\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a70e6291e4676598e602282ef2fba1240a067b87.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[hp=ap-ax\\]\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0ce86d85836f8acec9a8357b48de4823478dd4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\frac{ap-hp}{a}.\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" />\nTherefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/0/5b0b15738588d4d518421fe277ed45040aab84f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{hp}{b}=\\frac{ap-hp}{a}\\]\" width=\"109\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d46acf4e13ae60ab1344a9399e986903c6593799.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ahp=abp-bhp\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/530dc82ecfea9c940883635851a312d00d540cb4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ahp+bhp=abp\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d7c158932573cb0c9f0cb75e57624088822e090.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[hp(a+b)=abp\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/240df553ab47438515b7ed26d814b00fde141286.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h=\\frac{ab}{a+b},\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"39\" />\nas desired.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc779cb200fbc15c503e7049874b39ad6f0d1f8a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q.E.D.\\]\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb19deb279b5cc8f4c7d2ba8a426f3822480729c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\smiley\\]\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Coordinate.2Fanalytical_geometry_proof\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Coordinate/analytical_geometry_proof\">Coordinate/analytical geometry proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Two_poles_formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Coordinate/analytical geometry proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the same diagram as above, if we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the origin, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/e/a0e754392667fef01f4d2ce1b6d095c6d8fe797d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac2bd8c3fa7d56d5981772176cf3233764fe995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,b),(p,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc0eb1556968a81859ecb7afc518fe5c93088f0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p,a),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"20\" /> respectively. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> have slopes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a838399095809258aa56c5781270e7c8c9ac8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b-0}{0-p}=-\\frac{b}{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"98\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b6ca5524ff83e2ea00be2e62d60e9f960dd97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a-0}{p-0}=\\frac{a}{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"85\" height=\"42\" />, respectively, and y-intercepts of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/5085f53f913f21af1857d2767db27ee043ebe0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, respectively. That means their equations are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/c/3cc7e48d5a8bcff2469c4b4f9fcc843285c21892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\frac{b}{p}x+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"103\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b758dc608c50d427806cae0bb28077755171a29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{a}{p}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" />, respectively.\nSetting the two equations equal to find the intersection point(recall that a point is shared by two lines if and only if it satisfies the equation of both lines), we obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cec020bd93846b9d120cf217b437e1e56f90e2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-\\frac{b}{p}x+b=\\frac{a}{p}x\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/1/ab19f9f853384ca52f06c4f00286699340196621.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{b}{p}x+\\frac{a}{p}x=b\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5f284ba3d6dc85e50c517418799e7926e16a28c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\frac{a+b}{p})x=b\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/80333b467e60a6d679582a4ca2310be7f8afb800.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\frac{b}{\\frac{a+b}{p}}\\]\" width=\"63\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/c/9bc55954b9d24ca9c749258b00d6bb861356ce8a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\frac{bp}{a+b}.\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" />\nTo find the ordinate, we plug in this to either equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />(in this case, we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />'s equation because it contains fewer terms):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9099a344ac0afa7016cf34ac2235e08b6adcf1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=\\frac{a}{p}x=\\frac{a}{p} \\cdot \\frac{bp}{a+b}\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/8604c3bfd4c78f568884c98574bef259ebfecfb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=\\frac{abp}{p(a+b)}\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56b6700ae598d8af7ec25593ecdff692dd4e0bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=\\frac{ab}{a+b},\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the ordered pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94027b82e7115abadff4f018afd52db2729f871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{bp}{a+b},\\frac{ab}{a+b})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"111\" height=\"41\" />. Therefore, the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba12dc0fbbf04f35c0284b13e88fe6ccc7840490.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ab}{a+b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"42\" height=\"39\" />, as desired.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc779cb200fbc15c503e7049874b39ad6f0d1f8a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q.E.D.\\]\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Image_Credit\">Image Credit</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Two_poles_formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Image Credit\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://images.app.goo.gl/237wxi3A4qAEWNFW8\">https://images.app.goo.gl/237wxi3A4qAEWNFW8</a>\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Two_poles_formula&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017185125\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 258/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8455/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.479      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.479      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21871:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017185125 and revision id 238133. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}